abstract:
In this paper we strengthen to Morrey-Lorentz spaces the famous trace principle introduced by Adams. More precisely, we show that Riesz potential $I_{\alpha}$ is continuous  egin{equation} \Vert I_{\alpha}f\Vert_{\mathcal{M}_{q, \infty}^{\lambda_{\ast}}(d\mu)}\lesssim \Arrowvert\mu\Arrowvert_{ eta}^{{1}/{q}}\,\Vert f\Vert_{\mathcal{M}_{p, \infty}^{\lambda}(d
u)}
onumber\[0.02in] \end{equation} if and only if the Radon measure $d\mu$ supported in $\Omega\subset \mathbb{R}^n$ is controlled by $$\Arrowvert\mu\Arrowvert_{ eta}=\sup_{x\in\mathbb{R}^n,\,r>0}r^{- eta}\mu(B(x,r))<\infty$$ provided that $1<p<q<\infty$ satisfies $n-\alpha p< eta\leq n,\; \alpha= rac{n}{\lambda}- rac{ eta}{\lambda_\ast}\; 	ext{ and }\; rac{\lambda_\ast}{q}\leq  rac{\lambda}{p}
onumber\,$. Our result provide a new class of functions spaces which is larger than previous ones, since we have strict continuous inclusions $\dot{B}_{p,\infty}^{s}\hookrightarrow L^{\lambda, \infty}\hookrightarrow \mathcal{M}_{p}^{\lambda}\hookrightarrow\mathcal{M}_{p, \infty}^{\lambda} 
onumber $ as $1<p<\lambda<\infty$ and $s\in\mathbb{R}$ satisfies $ rac{1}{p}- rac{s}{n}= rac{1}{\lambda}$. If $d\mu$ is concentrated on $\partial\mathbb{R}^n_+$, as a byproduct we get Sobolev-Morrey trace inequality on half-spaces $\mathbb{R}^n_+$ which recovers the well-known Sobolev-trace inequality in $L^p(\mathbb{R}^n_+)$. Also, by a suitable analysis on non-doubling Cader'on-Zygmund decomposition we show that  egin{equation} \Vert M_{\alpha}f\Vert_{\mathcal{M}_{p, \ell}^{\lambda}(d\mu)}\,\sim\, \Vert I_{\alpha}f\Vert_{\mathcal{M}_{p, \ell}^{\lambda}(d\mu)}
onumber \end{equation} provided that $\mu(B_r(x))\sim r^{ eta}$ on support $	ext{spt}(\mu)$ and $n-\alpha < eta\leq n$ with $0<\alpha<n$. This result extends the previous ones.
